all, basketball, baseball, softball, track and field, golf, soccer, volleyball, and wrestling programs."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 539, "end": 605, "text": "The athletic programs compete in the Ohio Valley Conference (OVC)."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 606, "end": 657, "text": "The principal of Chesapeake is Chris Smith, and the"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 0, "end": 17, "text": "“Bye Bye Birdie”."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 18, "end": 159, "text": "In October 2007, Chesapeake High School was listed as one of four high schools in Anne Arundel County that had outbreaks of staph infections."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 160, "end": 289, "text": "28 cases of the infection have also been reported at Severna Park High School, Glen Burnie High School, and Old Mill High School."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 290, "end": 577, "text": "In February 2008, Chesapeake parents began an organization (CEEDSS) to protest a special education program, known as CRP or the Chesapeake Regional Program, that has been in the school since 1990, but according to parents has been disruptive to education and concealed by administration."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 578, "end": 615, "text": "Sports teams at Chesapeake, with both"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d04", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": ", Maryland ) ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d04", "start": 15, "end": 579, "text": "Public high school in Pasadena , Maryland , United States Chesapeake High School Address 4798 Mountain Road Pasadena , Maryland United States Coor